Server Side Public License, version 1 (SSPL-1.0) / Commercial
================================================================

This file and the software it governs -- the ``rotn-commercial`` paid layer
(``rot.commercial``: the Product 2 runtime coach **as a service**, the LangChain
adapter, the MCP ``tools/call`` gateway, the fleet near-miss aggregate, the G8
behavioral audit, and the Lethal-Trifecta risk surface) -- are **NOT** part of
the Apache-2.0 core.  They are distributed under the **Server Side Public
License, version 1 (SSPL-1.0)** and/or a **commercial license** issued by
CARAVEL.

Why a second license
--------------------
The **core** of ROTN (``rot`` -- the bounded engine, the spend-cap policy
class, the deterministic counterexample, the tests, the one-pager generator,
and the CI gate) is **Apache-2.0** (see the top-level ``LICENSE``): the proof
is open, that is the credibility wedge.

This **paid** layer is the value.  It is licensed so that a competitor who
offers a **hosted clone** of this layer must either (a) comply with the SSPL --
which requires offering the complete source of the *entire* hosted service
stack -- or (b) buy a commercial license from CARAVEL.  This is the legal
deterrent on the specific "hosted clone of my paid layer" threat.

What SSPL-1.0 adds over the core
--------------------------------
The one clause that matters for this layer is the **Additional Use Grant /
hosted-service obligation**: if you use this software to provide a service to
others, you must make available the complete source code of the **entire**
service (this software *and* every component of the hosting stack) under an
SSPL-compatible license.  The full, authoritative text of SSPL-1.0 is:

    https://www.mongodb.com/legal/licenses
    https://www.mongodb.com/about/legal/licenses/server-side-public-license/

A commercial license
--------------------
If you intend to use this layer in production or as a hosted service and
prefer the Apache-style permissive terms, or need to avoid the SSPL
hosted-service obligation, contact CARAVEL for a commercial license:

    https://github.com/caravel/rot-verify

